Emerging Life Sciences Trends Influencing the Market
In 2025, the animal genetics market is being shaped by rapid progress in genomics, gene editing, and data-driven breeding programs. Precision livestock farming is gaining momentum, integrating genetic insights with digital monitoring tools to optimize productivity and animal welfare.
The global push toward sustainable agriculture is also accelerating adoption of genetics that enhance feed efficiency and reduce environmental impact. Additionally, growing awareness around antimicrobial resistance is driving interest in disease-resistant animal breeds, positioning genetics as a frontline solution in modern livestock management.

Key Market Drivers
•	Rising global demand for meat, dairy, and animal protein, particularly in emerging economies
•	Advancements in genome sequencing and gene editing technologies, improving breeding precision
•	Government initiatives supporting food security and livestock modernization
•	Growing focus on disease resistance and reduced antibiotic usage
•	Expansion of large-scale commercial farming operations seeking productivity gains
Together, these factors are strengthening the role of animal genetics as a cornerstone of resilient and efficient agricultural systems.

